<section class="deck-slide" id="2" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="Slide 2 of 7" data-document-role="page" data-label="A cabin fire far from Earth can't wait for mission control" data-speaker-notes="The problem: delay. On Mars the one-way signal delay is about 12.5 minutes in our model, so any fire response has to happen locally. NASA's experiments (SAFFIRE, BASS, SOFIE, SAME, FLEX and more) tell us how flames behave in low gravity, low airflow and low oxygen. We built three connected parts: a research dashboard that ranks the evidence, an SI agent that uses it, and a live risk engine that watches the cabin."><div class="deck-fit"><div class="deck-scaler"><div style="width: 1920px; height: 1080px; position: relative; background: rgb(17, 26, 48); overflow: clip; contain: paint;" class="slide" data-canvas-width="1920" data-canvas-height="1080"><div data-frame-id="e0-ctvstt" style="position: absolute; inset: 0px; box-sizing: border-box;"><div data-node-path="" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 0px; width: 100%; height: 100%; padding: 80px 112px; box-sizing: border-box;"><div data-text-path="0" data-node-path="0" style="font-family: &quot;Space Grotesk&quot;, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.45; color: rgb(169, 182, 211); margin: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; text-wrap-style: pretty; min-width: 0px; min-height: 0px; flex-shrink: 0; letter-spacing: 3.6px; text-transform: uppercase; overflow-y: visible;">Introduction</div><div data-text-path="1" data-node-path="1" role="heading" aria-level="2" style="font-family: &quot;Space Grotesk&quot;, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 56px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; color: rgb(238, 242, 250); margin: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; text-wrap-style: pretty; min-width: 0px; min-height: 0px; flex-shrink: 0; padding: 0px 0px 36px; overflow-y: visible; box-sizing: border-box;">A cabin fire far from Earth can't wait for mission control</div><div data-node-path="2" style="display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: stretch; gap: 56px; min-width: 0px; min-height: 0px; flex-grow: 1; flex-basis: 0%;"><div data-node-path="2.0" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 28px; min-width: 620px; min-height: 0px; max-width: 620px;"><div data-text-path="2.0.0" data-node-path="2.0.0" style="font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.45; color: rgb(238, 242, 250); margin: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; text-wrap-style: pretty; min-width: 0px; min-height: 0px; flex-shrink: 0; opacity: 1; isolation: isolate; overflow-y: visible;">On a space station, Moon base or Mars habitat, a fire can spread before anyone on Earth even hears the alarm. A signal from Mars takes over 12 minutes one way.</div><div data-text-path="2.0.1" data-node-path="2.0.1" style="font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.45; color: rgb(169, 182, 211); margin: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: break-word; text-wrap-style: pretty; min-width: 0px; min-height: 0px; flex-shrink: 0; opacity: 1; isolation: isolate; overflow-y: visible;">NASA has flown many fire experiments in microgravity, but the findings sit in dense abstracts. Our dashboard turns them into evidence that crews and an autonomous agent can act on.</div><div data-node-path="2.0.2" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 0px; min-width: 0px; min-height: 0px; flex-shrink: 0; background-color: rgb(24, 35, 63); padding: 18px 28px; border-width: 0px 0px 0px 6px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(251, 138, 60); border-radius: 10px; opacity: 1; isolation: isolate; box-sizing: border-box;"><div data-text-path="2.0.2.0" data-node-path="2.0.2.0" style="font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, syst